                     <tr>
                        <td align="left" style="padding: 0px 18px 9px;">
                           <div style="text-align: center;">
                              <p style="font-size:18px; color:#ffffff; text-decoration: none;">
                                 Dear Customer,<br>
                              </p>
                              <p style="font-size:18px; color:#ffffff; text-decoration: none;">
                                 Thank you for applying for the Credit Card deferment. <br>
                              </p>
                              <p style="font-size:18px; color:#ffffff; text-decoration: none;">
                                 We would like to inform you that our team is currently reviewing your request. Once approved, the minimum payment on all your credit cards will be deferred for three months ( April, May, and June statements) <br>
                              </p>
                              <p style="font-size:18px; color:#ffffff; text-decoration: none;">
                                 During this time, you will not be required to make the minimum payment for the above statements; except past minimum dues. <br>
                              </p>
                              <p style="font-size:18px; color:#ffffff; text-decoration: none;">
                                 However, interest will continue to be charged on the outstanding balance.<br>
                              </p>
                              <p style="font-size:18px; color:#ffffff; text-decoration: none;">
                                 We will notify you once a decision has been made.<br>
                              </p>
                              <p style="font-size:18px; color:#ffffff; text-decoration: none;">
                                 If you have any questions or require further assistance, please contact us at 
                                 <a href="mailto:support@ilabank.com" style="color:#ffffff; text-decoration:none;">support@ilabank.com</a> or talk to us on 
                                 <a href="tel:+97317123456" style="color:#ffffff; text-decoration:none;">+973 17123456</a> 
                              </p>
                           </div>
                        </td>
                     </tr>
                     <tr>
                        <td style="padding-top:10px; padding-right:18px; padding-bottom:10px; padding-left:18px;" valign="top" align="center" class="mcnButtonBlockInner">
                           <table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="mcnButtonContentContainer" style="border-collapse: separate !important;border-radius: 30px;background-color: #79ED00;">
                              <tbody>
                                 <tr>
                                    <td align="center" valign="middle" class="mcnButtonContent" style="font-family:'Inter', 'Helvetica Neue', 'Helvetica', 'Arial', 'sans-serif'; font-size: 23px; padding: 12px 36px;">
                                       <a class="mcnButton " title="Open ila App" href="https://gateway.ilabank.com/redirect/mobile" target="_blank" style="font-weight: normal;letter-spacing: normal;line-height: 100%;text-align: center;text-decoration: none;color: #00153e;">Open ila App</a>
                                    </td>
                                 </tr>
                              </tbody>
                           </table>
                        </td>
                     </tr>
                     <br>
                     <tr>
                        <td align="left" style="padding: 0px 18px 9px;">
                           <div style="text-align: left;">
                              <p style="font-size:18px; color:#ffffff; text-decoration: none;">
                                 Terms and Condition : <br>
                              </p>
                              <ol style="padding-left: 10%; margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size:14px;">
                                 <li>Regulatory Basis</li>
                                 <ul style="list-style-position: inside; padding-left: 10%;  padding-top: 2%; padding-bottom: 2%; margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size:14px;">
                                    <li>ila Bank, the retail branch of Arab Banking Corporation B.S.C., licensed and regulated by the Central Bank of Bahrain (the “Bank”), offers this Credit Card payment deferment (“Payment Deferment”) as a temporary exceptional relief measure in line with applicable directives, guidance, and supervisory expectations issued by the Central Bank of Bahrain (“CBB”).</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">The Payment Deferment applies to all credit cards issued by the Bank (the “Credit Card(s)”) and does not constitute a waiver, concession, write off, or reduction of any amounts payable thereunder.</li>
                                 </ul>
                                 <li>Customer Request & Approval</li>
                                 <ul style="list-style-position: inside; padding-left: 10%;  padding-top: 2%; padding-bottom: 2%; margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size:14px;">
                                    <li>The Payment Deferment is available only upon the customer’s explicit request, and is subject to the Bank’s assessment and approval.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">The Bank reserves the right, at its sole discretion, to determine eligibility, approve or decline requests, and impose conditions in accordance with regulatory requirements.</li>
                                 </ul>
                                 <li>Scope & Duration of Deferment</li>
                                 <ul style="list-style-position: inside; padding-left: 10%;  padding-top: 2%; padding-bottom: 2%; margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size:14px;">
                                    <li>Upon approval, the Payment Deferment shall apply for three (3) consecutive billing cycles (“Deferment Period”).</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">For the current implementation, the Deferment Period shall only cover the statement months of April, May, and June.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">The Payment Deferment shall apply to all Credit Card(s) issued by the Bank to the customer, including primary and supplementary cards, unless otherwise determined by the Bank.</li>
                                 </ul>
                                 <li>Minimum Payment Obligation</li>
                                 <ul style="list-style-position: inside; padding-left: 10%;  padding-top: 2%; padding-bottom: 2%; margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size:14px;">
                                    <li>During the Deferment Period, the customer shall not be required to make the Minimum Payment Due reflected in the applicable monthly Credit Card statement(s).</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">The total outstanding balance shall continue to be disclosed in the Credit Card statement(s) for transparency and monitoring purposes.</li>
                                 </ul>
                                 <li>Exclusion of Past Due Amounts</li>
                                 <ul style="list-style-position: inside; padding-left: 10%;  padding-top: 2%; padding-bottom: 2%; margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size:14px;">
                                    <li>Any overdue minimum payments or arrears existing prior to the effective date of the Payment Deferment shall not be covered by the deferment.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">Such overdue amounts shall continue to appear in the Credit Card statement(s) and remain payable in accordance with the Bank’s Credit Card Terms and Conditions.</li>
                                 </ul>
                                 <li>Interest Accrual</li>
                                 <ul style="list-style-position: inside; padding-left: 10%;  padding-top: 2%; padding-bottom: 2%; margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size:14px;">
                                    <li>Notwithstanding the deferment of the Minimum Payment Due, interest shall continue to accrue on all outstanding balances on the Credit Card(s) throughout the Deferment Period.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">Interest shall be calculated on existing balances and any transactions incurred during the Deferment Period in accordance with the approved rates and the Bank’s Schedule of Fees and Charges, as amended from time to time.</li>
                                 </ul>
                                 <li>Use of Credit Card(s)</li>
                                 <ul style="list-style-position: inside; padding-left: 10%;  padding-top: 2%; padding-bottom: 2%; margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size:14px;">
                                    <li>Customers may continue to use all Credit Card(s) during the Deferment Period, subject to available credit limits and the Bank’s standard policies.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">All new transactions shall be subject to applicable interest, fees, and charges in accordance with the Credit Card Terms and Conditions.</li>
                                 </ul>
                                 <li>Easy Payment Plans</li>
                                 <ul style="list-style-position: inside; padding-left: 10%;  padding-top: 2%; padding-bottom: 2%; margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size:14px;">
                                    <li>Where an Easy Payment Plan is active on any Credit Card, the remaining plan tenure shall be extended by three (3) months, corresponding to the Deferment Period.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">The installment amount and applicable interest rate shall otherwise remain unchanged.</li>
                                 </ul>
                                 <li>Resumption of Normal Payments</li>
                                 <ul style="list-style-position: inside; padding-left: 10%;  padding-top: 2%; padding-bottom: 2%; margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size:14px;">
                                    <li>Upon expiry of the Deferment Period, normal minimum payment obligations shall automatically resume without further notice.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">The customer shall be required to make payments as reflected in subsequent Credit Card statement(s), including amounts accumulated during the Deferment Period.</li>
                                 </ul>
                                 <li>Credit Classification & Reporting</li>
                                 <ul style="list-style-position: inside; padding-left: 10%;  padding-top: 2%; padding-bottom: 2%; margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size:14px;">
                                    <li>During an approved and active Deferment Period, the Credit Card account(s) shall not be treated as delinquent solely due to participation in the Payment Deferment, provided the customer complies with these Terms & Conditions.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">Failure to meet payment obligations after the Deferment Period may result in adverse credit classification and reporting to relevant credit bureau, in accordance with applicable laws, regulations, and CBB requirements.</li>
                                 </ul>
                                 <li>General Provisions</li>
                                 <ul style="list-style-position: inside; padding-left: 10%;  padding-top: 2%; padding-bottom: 2%; margin: 0; text-align: left; font-size:14px;">
                                    <li>A customer shall be ineligible for the Payment Deferment if, at the time of application or at any time thereafter, the customer (i) has any past-due, delinquent, unpaid, or legally recoverable amounts owing to the Bank, whether matured or unmatured, disputed or undisputed; or (ii) is subject to, involved in, or threatened with any ongoing or pending legal action, claim, investigation, judgment, enforcement action, insolvency proceeding, or other legal or administrative proceeding relating to any financial obligation. The Bank shall have the sole and absolute discretion to determine eligibility and may deny, suspend, or revoke the Payment Deferment at any time.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">The Payment Deferment is a temporary regulatory relief measure and may be amended, suspended, or withdrawn by the Bank in accordance with CBB directives.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">These Terms & Conditions shall be read together with the ila Bank Credit Card Terms and Conditions, which shall continue to apply in full.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">In the event of any inconsistency, the ila Bank Credit Card Terms and Conditions shall prevail.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">The Payment Deferment shall not create any precedent, expectation, or right for the customer to receive similar relief or deferment in the future.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">The Payment Deferment shall not be construed as an amendment, novation, or variation of the Credit Card agreement, except to the limited extent expressly stated herein.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">The Bank reserves the right to cancel the Payment Deferment with immediate effect if the customer is found to have provided incorrect information, misused the facility, or breached these Terms & Conditions.</li>
                                    <li style="padding-top: 2%;">The Payment Deferment remains subject at all times to applicable directives and instructions issued by the Central Bank of Bahrain, which shall prevail in the event of any conflict.</li>
                                 </ul>
                              </ol>
                              <p style="font-size:18px; color:#ffffff; text-decoration: none;">
                                 Best Regards, <br>
                                 ila Bank
                              </p>
                           </div>
                        </td>
                     </tr>
